// Volumes: slices in position order.
//
// The default `volume3d` rule keeps the default instance order
// (InstanceNumber). InstanceNumber does not always follow the position of the
// slice, so the stack order and the volume order can differ.
//
// This file changes the `sortBy` of `volume3d`: the slices of each display set
// are in the order of `sliceDistance`, the distance along the normal of the
// image plane, from one origin for the series. An image that is not in the main
// plane has no distance, and goes after the images that have one.
//
// The rule keeps its id and its place, so a hanging protocol that selects
// `splitRuleId` `volume3d` still finds the display sets. The file changes only
// `sortBy`, so it works together with `byAcquisition`, in either order.
{
  "displaySetRules": {
    "volume3d": {
      "sortBy": { "$set": ["displaySet.sliceDistance", "InstanceNumber"] }
    }
  }
}
